## Project Overview
HeatWave PvP (`two-plus-one-jack-web`) is a real-time multiplayer crash game built on PixiJS v8 (WebGL/WebGPU). Players compete in duel (1v1) and tournament formats across 10 white-label partners (Ember, GamerSaloon, Sparket, Kaboom, FreeWin, BlockHead, Butr, MidoLotto, Speed, Toast). The game is served as a WebView embedded inside partner mobile apps and communicates with the host app via a postMessage bridge.

## Tech Stack
- **Renderer**: PixiJS v8 (`pixi.js` ^8.3.4) — WebGL/WebGPU canvas rendering
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode, `noUnusedLocals`, `noUnusedParameters`, `noImplicitReturns`)
- **Build**: Vite 5 with EJS templates per game mode
- **Animation**: GSAP 3 (`gsap` ^3.12.5)
- **Real-time**: Socket.IO client 4 (`socket.io-client` ^4.7.5)
- **Audio**: Howler.js via `@pixi/sound` ^6.0.1
- **HTTP**: Axios ^1.7.7
- **Error monitoring**: Sentry (`@sentry/browser` ^8.33.1)
- **Animations**: Lottie Web (`lottie-web` ^5.12.2)
- **Analytics**: Microsoft Clarity (via `clarity.init.ts`)
- **Logging**: Custom `Logger` class with IndexedDB persistence + S3 upload (`idb` ^8.0.0)
- **Auth**: JWT query param (`?at=...`), decoded with `jwt-decode` ^4.0.0

